        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "042a5c95-d550-340f-883a-c5cafe5f2c6b",
                "word": "aporie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "81e84100-6ca0-47bd-83b8-bcac52313c4b",
                        "entry_id": "042a5c95-d550-340f-883a-c5cafe5f2c6b",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "apories"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                        "entry_id": "042a5c95-d550-340f-883a-c5cafe5f2c6b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Problème ou contradiction logique insoluble."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "formal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "44860ac9-df2b-4af0-b3bb-4f1648f1d041",
                                "sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                                "text": "Mais, dupé par la langue grecque, qui, grâce à l’article, permet de transformer des verbes en substantifs, il n’échappe à l’aporie de Parménide « L’Être est, le non-être n’est pas, on ne sortira pas de cette pensée » que par cinq théories […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "24640242-d502-404f-a259-f73f451552b5",
                                "sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                                "text": "Devrons-nous, comme Jonathan Barnes, retenir l’image d’une pensée campant résolument dans l’aporie qu’elle aurait osé formuler ? (« le scepticisme abdéritain est de type pyrrhonien », déclare expressément cet auteur)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa1b3b02-16c8-472f-a261-ed24af0c20b9",
                                "sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                                "text": "L’aporie est une espèce d’énigme, mais considérée d’un point de vue logique plutôt que magique ou spirituel. C’est un problème qu’on renonce à résoudre, au moins provisoirement, ou un mystère qu’on refuse d’adorer."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a87fbff2-fc4f-4052-b715-ea7024c1cf21",
                                "sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                                "text": "Aucun néo-humain, je le savais maintenant, ne serait en mesure de trouver une solution à l’aporie constitutive ; ceux qui l'avaient tenté, s'il y en avait eu, étaient probablement déjà morts."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a36a43cd-8e74-40cf-8c6d-6662c9838aa9",
                                "sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                                "text": "L’équation semble une aporie. Elle l’est en logique. Elle cesse de l’être en démocratie. C’est l’éthique qui en offre l’issue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e5bb1cb-85ea-4735-bf28-c56cad5800f7",
                                "sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                                "text": "Et la faisabilité juridique d’une consultation unique portant sur un marché expérimental et un marché de droit commun reste à confirmer ; l’aporie tenant à retenir in fine un MGP classique quand l’étude préalable a établi le bilan plus favorable du MGP expérimental reste à dépasser."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1d0bb1be-024d-49c0-b231-8d00f00fc04d",
                        "source_entry_id": "042a5c95-d550-340f-883a-c5cafe5f2c6b",
                        "source_sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                        "target_lang_word": "Aporie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Aporie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b10b4a1d-df9e-316a-ad22-39c00111b8b7",
                                        "entry_id": "01c303d0-305b-32ad-8d89-e77cf8e43dcd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Ratlosigkeit, die Ausweglosigkeit"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "general"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d64c2f2f-e643-4b0f-b8e0-38f7c20dd302",
                                                "sense_id": "b10b4a1d-df9e-316a-ad22-39c00111b8b7",
                                                "text": "Wir befinden uns oft in einer Aporie zwischen „Abwarten“ und „Handeln“."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4048f49-a626-3cce-9106-c9f141e6dd7b",
                                        "entry_id": "01c303d0-305b-32ad-8d89-e77cf8e43dcd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "die Unmöglichkeit, zur Auflösung eines Problems zu gelangen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d05152c1-04d0-492a-a5bf-84b25e601759",
                                                "sense_id": "b4048f49-a626-3cce-9106-c9f141e6dd7b",
                                                "text": "„Auf dem Hintergrund der Aporien von Dualismus und psycho-physischem Parallelismus, die eine Beeinflussung von materiellen und geistigen Prozessen ausschließen, formulierte De La Mettrie zum ersten Mal einen materialistischen Monismus: Alle seelischen Regungen haben eine physiologische Ursache; […]“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d85ecce8-c208-4fdb-b7b4-f46bbe924664",
                        "source_entry_id": "042a5c95-d550-340f-883a-c5cafe5f2c6b",
                        "source_sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                        "target_lang_word": "aporia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aporia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0e923c5-ce8f-32f1-a34e-dab3196aeb37",
                                        "entry_id": "d36ca907-6526-3b86-b083-9ea37b071b37",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An expression of deliberation with oneself regarding uncertainty or doubt as to how to proceed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "rhetoric"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0215aa74-da71-4957-860d-1a5a4d615ba5",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e923c5-ce8f-32f1-a34e-dab3196aeb37",
                                                "text": "Aporia oft in doubt and fear will rest,\nAnd reason with itself what may be best."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51fbab24-17ec-4aa4-b7b6-279efec4800b",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e923c5-ce8f-32f1-a34e-dab3196aeb37",
                                                "text": "Meanings are superposed in an aporia – not ‘either/or’, but ‘and/and’."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2618bc9-a6dc-458b-a155-53cce4d7231b",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e923c5-ce8f-32f1-a34e-dab3196aeb37",
                                                "text": "What they intend sickens and frightens them, and they can never speak of it directly. Instead, wrapped in whispers are ellipses, euphemisms, mumbled aporia followed by throat-clearing and a brisk change of subject."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e011b54-bec7-3fd0-9815-4a8633f59d8c",
                                        "entry_id": "d36ca907-6526-3b86-b083-9ea37b071b37",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An insoluble contradiction, especially in a text's meaning; a logical impasse suggested by a text or speaker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "73b5a6de-f32d-408a-a99e-b8e8f0fe1481",
                                                "sense_id": "8e011b54-bec7-3fd0-9815-4a8633f59d8c",
                                                "text": "EL James's multimillion selling series of novels ‘encodes the aporias of heterosexual relationships’, according to Professor Eva Illouz[.]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fd473ae-2568-4344-8641-0372c1461d35",
                                                "sense_id": "8e011b54-bec7-3fd0-9815-4a8633f59d8c",
                                                "text": "But Green issues are already a contested zone, already a site where politicization is being fought for. In what follows, I want to stress two other aporias in capitalist realism, which are not yet politicized to anything like the same degree. The first is mental health."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d6c238d-355c-46d2-aede-2f761428735e",
                                                "sense_id": "8e011b54-bec7-3fd0-9815-4a8633f59d8c",
                                                "text": "Plato believed that the core impulse to philosophizing lies in aporia, the point at which, in struggling to understand a phenomenon or answer a question, we come up against a seemingly irresolvable contradiction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ec6e75a0-240f-4d37-aa3b-a6e62cba2eb1",
                        "source_entry_id": "042a5c95-d550-340f-883a-c5cafe5f2c6b",
                        "source_sense_id": "07d55a2d-8055-3128-89bc-896a0a480909",
                        "target_lang_word": "aporía",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "aporía",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e44cd444-f775-3de4-a000-b8c8fe1db88f",
                                        "entry_id": "d1256aa0-87b3-395d-b4ab-4fa322519cc1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Problema insoluble o que no tiene solución viable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f42cd384-9b76-4f1f-b5b7-6d73df95cdce",
                                                "sense_id": "e44cd444-f775-3de4-a000-b8c8fe1db88f",
                                                "text": "Diodoro Cronos, por ejemplo, modificó las leyes racionalmente imposibles (aporías) de Zenón de Elea para negar así el movimiento de las cosas."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6d22b13-baf8-3c98-abe8-2d232aadb102",
                                        "entry_id": "d1256aa0-87b3-395d-b4ab-4fa322519cc1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Paradoja, contradicción o imposibilidad a la que se llega a partir de ciertas premisas o suposiciones."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
